    "q-2980": {
      "dom_id": "step-q2980",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "The equation ${log}_{5}⁡25=2$ is equivalent to ${5}^{x}=25.$ Determine the value of $x.$",
      "worked_solution": "The logarithm of $a$ with base $b$ is defined as follows:\n\n${log}_{b}⁡a=x$ is equivalent to $a={b}^{x}$\n\nIf we compare ${log}_{5}⁡25=2$ with ${log}_{b}⁡a=x,$ we get $a=25,$ $b=5,$ and $x=2.$\n\nTherefore, the given equation is equivalent to ${5}^{2}=25.$ Consequently, $x=2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
