    "q-252568": {
      "dom_id": "step-q252568",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "If the equation ${log}_{9}⁡9=1$ is equivalent to ${b}^{1}=9,$  then $b=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The logarithm of $a$ with base $b$ is defined as follows:\n\n${log}_{b}⁡a=x$ is equivalent to $a={b}^{x}$\n\nIf we compare ${log}_{9}⁡9=1$ with ${log}_{b}⁡a=x,$ we get $a=9,$ $b=9,$ and $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, the given equation is equivalent to ${9}^{1}=9.$ Consequently, $b=9.$",
