    "q-66712": {
      "dom_id": "step-q66712",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "The equation ${log}_{64}⁡4=\\frac{1}{3}$ is equivalent to $\\sqrt[3]{b}=4.$ What is the value of $b?$",
      "worked_solution": "The logarithm of $a$ with base $b$ is defined as follows:\n\n${log}_{b}⁡a=x$ is equivalent to $a={b}^{x}$\n\nIf we compare ${log}_{64}⁡4=\\frac{1}{3}$ with ${log}_{b}⁡a=x,$ we get $a=4,$ $b=64,$ and $x=\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the given equation is equivalent to ${64}^{1/3}=4,$ which is also equivalent to $\\sqrt[3]{64}=4.$ Consequently, $b=64.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-66712-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "64",
              "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"84\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c36\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c34\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>64</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>"
            },
