    "q-252634": {
      "dom_id": "step-q252634",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Express the equation ${log}_{5}⁡(\\frac{1}{125})=-3$ in exponential form. Write the exponential term on the left-hand side of the equation.\n\n{{field-1}}$=$\n{{field-2}}",
      "worked_solution": "The logarithm of $a$ with base $b$ is defined as follows:\n\n${log}_{b}⁡a=x$ is equivalent to $a={b}^{x}$\n\nIf we compare ${log}_{5}⁡(\\frac{1}{125})=-3$ with ${log}_{b}⁡a=x,$ we get $a=\\frac{1}{125},$ $b=5,$ and $x=-3.$\n\nTherefore, the given equation is equivalent to \n\n$$\n{5}^{-3}=\\frac{1}{125}.\n$$",
